# VTID-03942 — commands run during this change

## Investigation (via Explore subagent, then independently verified)
Confirmed the exact bug by reading both files directly:
$ grep -n "is_sold_out\|isSoldOut" src/pages/PublicCampaignLanding.tsx
  181:    isSoldOut: false, // TODO: Fetch from event data
$ grep -n "is_sold_out" src/pages/PublicEventLanding.tsx
  33:  is_sold_out?: boolean;
  169:    isSoldOut: event?.is_sold_out || false,
Confirmed the CTA label rendering site (line 407, {ctaConfig.label}) and
the exact label strings in src/lib/eventsCtaUtils.ts's
getLocalizedLabel()/getPublicLandingCta() — 'Sold Out' when isSoldOut,
'Buy Ticket' (plain, no price suffix) only when lowestPrice is
null/undefined, otherwise 'Buy Ticket · <price>'.

## Fix
services/../src/pages/PublicCampaignLanding.tsx:
1. Added `is_sold_out: boolean` to LinkedEventTicketInfo.
2. Added `is_sold_out: event.is_sold_out || false` to the
   setLinkedEventTickets(...) call.
3. Changed `isSoldOut: false` to
   `isSoldOut: linkedEventTickets?.is_sold_out || false`.

## New test file (written from scratch)
src/pages/PublicCampaignLanding.test.tsx — 2 tests, no existing test file
for this page before this VTID. Mocks:
- react-router-dom (useParams/useNavigate/useSearchParams)
- @/integrations/supabase/client (supabase.rpc, supabase.from) — NO live
  network/Supabase calls, per this repo's absolute rule
- @/context/AuthProvider, @/hooks/useTranslation, @/lib/i18n-toast,
  @/lib/locale-format, @/components/SEO, @/components/tickets/EventTicketSelector

Caught one real assertion bug before finalizing: the non-sold-out test's
fixture initially set lowest_ticket_price: 25, which makes
getLocalizedPublicLandingCta render "Buy Ticket · $25.00" (via the
buyTicketWithPrice branch), not plain "Buy Ticket" — the
`screen.getByText('Buy Ticket')` assertion would have failed for a reason
unrelated to the fix under test. Set lowest_ticket_price: null in that
fixture instead, with an inline comment explaining why.

